  "result": {
    "summary": "A six-dose frozen development scan selected scale0.01, then 16,384 disjoint confirmation hands showed only 0.81-1.74% greedy disagreement and positive generic-anchor deltas, including positive lower bounds versus uniform and min-bet. The direct Standard10 delta was -1.0010 bb/100, CI [-9.5199,7.5180], so the preregistered learned-anchor gate failed.",
    "conclusion": "Posthoc shrinkage converts the scale1 residual into a genuinely preservation-compatible policy and its generic exploit gains replicate, but it does not establish improvement over the mature learned reference. The frozen candidate is rejected for promotion and Slumbot.",
    "decision": "REJECT_FROZEN_RESIDUAL_SCALE_TRANSFER",
    "next_step": "Run at most one matched small-root control that trains the residual under scale0.01 visitation rather than scale1 then posthoc shrinkage, and evaluate on learned-policy anchors; stop this route if the learned-anchor direction does not improve."
  },
